Spec: Revocation budget verification

Purpose:
  Exercise reservation admission and revocation at hard operation limits using owned temporary state.

Owns:
  ./CapacityTests.cs

Must:
  Remove newer connection journals when constructing older schema fixtures; migration must not invent flows or attachments.
  Remove newer access tables when constructing historical schema fixtures and verify the current schema version after migration.
  Verify global and host limits, multiple approved declarations, restart, historical replay and non-approved revocation.
  Prove failed writes retain the reservation and concurrent writers cannot spend it twice or oversubscribe capacity.
  Verify schema-two migration preserves decisions/results when reservations fit and rolls back when they do not.
  Keep native storage failures and untested physical disk exhaustion outside the logical reservation claim.
